GeoCeDG licensing scope

GeoCeDG is a composite source distribution and application. No single license
applies to every file or to the complete packaged product.

1. GeoCeDG-authored software

Unless a file carries a valid different notice, software source and
software-oriented scripts authored for GeoCeDG are made available under the
European Union Public Licence, version 1.2 (EUPL-1.2). The exact text is in
LICENSES/EUPL-1.2.txt. This grant does not replace or alter notices attached to
inherited GeoGebra source or independent third-party files.

2. GeoCeDG-authored documentation

Unless a document states an exception, GeoCeDG-authored documentation is made
available under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0).
The exact text is in LICENSES/CC-BY-4.0.txt and the scope and exceptions are
recorded in docs/LICENSE.md.

3. GeoCeDG-authored artwork and official marks

Ordinary GeoCeDG-authored artwork is made available under CC BY 4.0 when its
asset record selects that licensing class. The current official application
icon and splash artwork are author-owned; their versioned provenance and
copyright class are recorded in geocedg/resources/assets-manifest.yml.

Copyright permission for artwork is distinct from permission to use the
GeoCeDG name or official product marks. The author-approved brand-use rules
are in docs/licensing/trademark-policy.md. The Spanish denominative-mark
application `M4403138` has been filed and remains pending; that filing is not a
registration grant and is independent from artwork copyright licensing.

4. Inherited GeoGebra material

GeoGebra-authored software source is governed by EUPL-1.2. GeoGebra Language
Files, documentation, user-interface images and style files, and other
GeoGebra Materials are separately governed by GeoGebra's applicable terms,
including CC BY-NC-SA 4.0-or-later and non-commercial product conditions. See
LICENSES/GeoGebra-License-2025-11.md and LICENSES/CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0.txt.
GeoGebra names and marks remain separate rights. GeoCeDG is an independent
fork and is not endorsed by GeoGebra GmbH.

5. Independent third-party components

Third-party libraries, native binaries, fonts and resources retain their own
terms. LICENSES/manifest.json identifies the exact legal texts in the bundle;
THIRD_PARTY.md and geocedg/validation/pre-g9b-d1/component-disposition.json
record component-specific evidence and unresolved cases.

6. Complete binary/package

The complete package combines the classes above. It is not licensed solely
under EUPL-1.2 and must not be described globally as Open Source or Free
Software while non-commercial GeoGebra Materials/Language Files remain in the
payload. PROFILE NC is the approved deployability profile for the exact audited
composition and remains non-commercial only.

INTERNAL EVALUATION — NOT FOR REDISTRIBUTION

PRE-G9B-D1 is PASS — AUTHOR APPROVED, but this does not retitle or publish the
current `0.9.0` internal-evaluation package. Public package-state/version
materialization belongs to a later explicit step. Commercial distribution is
not authorized and remains dependent on external terms recorded in
docs/licensing/geocedg_profile_commercial.md.
